# TypeScript (repo-specific)

Prefer ESLint + `npx tsc --noEmit` for general style. Keep these local conventions:

## Components

- Prefer function declarations over `React.FC`
- Simple one-offs: inline props are fine
- Shared UI: extract prop types; extend DOM with `React.ComponentProps<"element">`

```tsx
// ✅ Good
export function Hero() { ... }

// ❌ Avoid
export const Hero: React.FC = () => { ... }

type ButtonProps = React.ComponentProps<"button"> & {
  variant?: "primary" | "secondary";
};
```

## Imports

Use `import type` for type-only imports:

```tsx
import { clsx, type ClassValue } from "clsx";
import type { VariantProps } from "class-variance-authority";
```

## `any` and lazy routes

Avoid `any` unless a third-party type or a documented workaround forces it. For `lazyWithRetry`, constrain the generic at the call site rather than widening with `any`.

```tsx
// Prefer a tight constraint over ComponentType<any>
function lazyWithRetry<T extends ComponentType<Record<string, unknown>>>(
  importFn: () => Promise<{ default: T }>,
  retries = 1
): React.LazyExoticComponent<T> { ... }
```

## Errors

```tsx
catch (error) {
  const err = error instanceof Error ? error : new Error(String(error));
}
```

